WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:15.225
and Mandy could not believe their eyes.

2
00:00:16.406 --> 00:00:18.548
They followed Charlotte through the factory.

3
00:00:19.828 --> 00:00:25.452
Every room was filled with factory workers: men, women, and children.

4
00:00:25.472 --> 00:00:30.516
"Florence, why are children working in the factory?"

5
00:00:31.696 --> 00:00:32.397
asked Mandy.

6
00:00:33.517 --> 00:00:35.238
Florence's face was serious.

7
00:00:35.258 --> 00:00:39.481
"For their families, Miss Mandy," she said.

8
00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:45.404
"People want British products, so our factories must stay busy.

9
00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:50.327
That means everyone, including poor children, must work."

10
00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:55.770
It didn't seem fair to Mandy, but she kept quiet.

11
00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.512
Loud noises came from a nearby room.

12
00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:06.554
They went in and saw huge machines with big metal rollers moving back and forth.

13
00:01:06.574 --> 00:01:10.795
"They look like mechanical weaving machines!"

14
00:01:13.295 --> 00:01:15.736
Mandy cried, but no one heard her.

15
00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:21.318
The sound was so loud that she had to put her fingers in her ears.

16
00:01:21.338 --> 00:01:23.498
"Miss Charlotte!"

17
00:01:23.998 --> 00:01:27.139
yelled a man carrying a stack of paper under one arm.

18
00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:29.892
"Mr. Geoffrey!

19
00:01:29.912 --> 00:01:34.635
I want to see my father," Charlotte yelled over the noise.

20
00:01:35.675 --> 00:01:38.417
The man turned and led them out of the noisy room.

21
00:01:38.437 --> 00:01:43.300
"He is very busy, Miss Charlotte," said Mr.

22
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.921
Geoffrey. "He can't see you now."

23
00:01:47.242 --> 00:01:48.883
Charlotte looked very sad.

24
00:01:48.903 --> 00:01:52.605
"I want him to meet Vinnie and Mandy."

25
00:01:54.126 --> 00:01:55.827
Mr. Geoffrey shook his head.

26
00:01:55.847 --> 00:01:59.649
"Please," pleaded Charlotte.

27
00:01:59.669 --> 00:02:03.171
"I'm sorry, no," said Mr.

28
00:02:03.211 --> 00:02:06.312
Geoffrey. "What are you making here?"

29
00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:07.493
Vinnie asked.

30
00:02:07.513 --> 00:02:10.375
"This is a textile factory.

31
00:02:11.435 --> 00:02:15.177
We weave cloth and make clothes," replied Mr.

32
00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:19.440
Geoffrey. "Do all the factories here make clothes?"

33
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.301
asked Mandy.

34
00:02:21.321 --> 00:02:26.824
"No, across the street, they make parts for the railroad," he said.

35
00:02:28.336 --> 00:02:30.877
"Why are there so many factories?"

36
00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.218
Mandy wanted to know.

37
00:02:34.719 --> 00:02:36.099
Mr. Geoffrey laughed.

38
00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.280
"The world is changing.

39
00:02:39.621 --> 00:02:40.861
Industry is the future!

40
00:02:42.042 --> 00:02:44.263
If you need something, England can make it."

41
00:02:45.443 --> 00:02:50.566
Since Charlotte was not allowed to see her father, she wanted to leave.

42
00:02:51.846 --> 00:02:55.708
So they left the factory and found the cab driver waiting.

43
00:02:57.604 --> 00:02:59.325
Suddenly, church bells rang.

44
00:03:00.665 --> 00:03:03.647
Vinnie turned to see a large bell tower in the distance.

45
00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.847
"That is St.

46
00:03:05.887 --> 00:03:13.851
Katherine's, an old church that escaped the Great Fire in 1666," Florence said proudly.

47
00:03:13.871 --> 00:03:20.653
"The fire destroyed over 87 churches in London, but not St.

48
00:03:20.673 --> 00:03:23.654
Katherine's!" "Let's go.

49
00:03:24.075 --> 00:03:25.055
It's teatime!"

50
00:03:26.175 --> 00:03:27.216
demanded Charlotte.

51
00:03:28.488 --> 00:03:30.209
She turned to Vinnie and Mandy.

52
00:03:30.229 --> 00:03:33.709
"Would you like to come to my home for tea?"

53
00:03:33.729 --> 00:03:37.631
"We'd love to," they replied.

54
00:03:39.091 --> 00:03:42.492
They got into the carriage and rode toward Charlotte's house.

55
00:03:43.812 --> 00:03:48.093
As they passed through the streets, the city changed again.

56
00:03:48.113 --> 00:03:53.635
"How clean and pretty the streets are," Mandy thought.

57
00:03:54.915 --> 00:03:57.336
The houses here were bigger and nicer too.

58
00:03:58.896 --> 00:04:02.101
Charlotte's house was on a square with several other homes.

59
00:04:03.423 --> 00:04:06.006
A pretty garden was in the middle of the square.

60
00:04:07.168 --> 00:04:09.291
Little children were playing outside.

61
00:04:09.311 --> 00:04:15.739
"What a difference from the other side of London," Mandy said to herself.
